&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FULL-TIME JOB VACANCY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology, Rights and Investigations Division&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multiple Office Locations Considered&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deadline: December 13, 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Human Rights Watch (HRW) is seeking a highly qualified Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence to investigate, analyze, and advocate against human rights abuses worldwide related to artificial intelligence. The role of the Senior Researcher will include documenting and conveying the rights implications of various forms of artificial intelligence and other algorithmic decision-making being developed and deployed by governments and private sector actors around the world for exclusion and repression, including &amp;nbsp;information control and censorship and discriminatory decision making, especially in high-risk contexts, for example by law enforcement and immigration authorities. Experience working on the impact of AI or other technology issues in Asia is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits in the Tech and Human Rights team within the broader Technology, Rights and Investigations Division and will report to the Deputy Director based in New York. The Senior Researcher on Human Rights and Artificial Intelligence will collaborate with other team members in the Technology, Rights and Investigations Division, and colleagues in regional and thematic divisions, and other relevant departments of HRW, including media, legal and policy team, and the advocacy department.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have deep domain expertise, as well as a track record of conducting&amp;nbsp;research and investigations at the intersection of human rights abuses and AI. The role will be based in any of the following locations where HRW has an office, and will be expected to work from the office on an as-needed basis: New York, Washington DC, Los Angeles, San Francisco, Toronto, Sao Paulo, London, Brussels, Amsterdam, Berlin, Nairobi, Johannesburg, Beirut, or Stockholm.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Develop a plan for strategic research and advocacy for influencing the development, application, and regulation of artificial intelligence and similar technologies by governments and the private sector to ensure respect for internationally recognized human rights, including non-discrimination and accountability;&lt;br&gt;2. Research, document, and analyze policies and practices related to AI, machine learning, and big data technologies that raise human rights concerns by collecting and analyzing information from a wide variety of sources, including governments, media, academia, NGOs, victims of abuses, open-source information, technologists, and others; Interview persons whose rights have been harmed by AI technologies, as well as related professionals and experts (e.g., organizations representing impacted communities, engineers who build AI technologies, data and computer scientists, etc.);&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;3. Identify and document where use of AI may have disparate impact on vulnerable or marginalized groups or may exacerbate economic inequality, and place abuses or potential for abuses within the broader political, social and economic contexts;&lt;br&gt;4. Write and publicize reports, op-eds, press releases, briefing memos, statements, testimony and other materials to disseminate our research findings and policy recommendations for preventing or ending human rights abuses linked to artificial intelligence applications;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;5. Work with colleagues in the Communications Department to develop innovative multimedia and social media strategies to communicate our positions in clear and compelling ways and to advance advocacy;&lt;br&gt;6. Develop and implement advocacy strategies in collaboration with HRW colleagues to change or prevent abusive government laws, policies, and practices, as well as abusive corporate policies and practices;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;7. Press companies and governments to ensure human rights protections are built into artificial intelligence by design from the outset and articulate how existing human rights standards should apply to emerging AI technologies; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;8. Build partnerships across key communities, including other human rights NGOs, groups representing vulnerable populations, data scientists, machine learning programmers, tech industry leaders, and academics;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;9. Contribute to the shaping of public debates on AI around human rights internationally through clear and prompt responses to queries from policy makers, the media, colleagues, and human rights communities;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;10. Work collaboratively with an international team of researchers within the Technology, Rights and Investigations division, including the Digital Investigations Lab, other thematic and country HRW researchers, and other relevant departments of HRW, including Communications, Legal and Policy, Advocacy, and the General Counsel’s office;&lt;br&gt;11. Travel domestically and internationally, as required, to conduct research, media work and advocacy; and&lt;br&gt;12. Be prepared and willing to work flexible hours to accommodate developing and urgent events;&lt;br&gt;13. Carry out other tasks as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates who are traditionally underrepresented in the technology and/or human rights sectors&amp;nbsp;(such as people who identify as BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, women, migrants, people with disabilities, or people who have other related lived experiences) are enthusiastically encouraged to apply if they feel they have the ability to succeed in this role, even if they do not have all the skills and qualifications listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; An advanced degree in journalism, law, public policy, national security, computer science, or a related field or equivalent experience is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; A minimum of seven years of experience is required. This experience could come from a&lt;br&gt;variety of previous roles including, but not limited to journalists who have covered technology,&lt;br&gt;community activism, work at impact litigation organizations, academics, or industry professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Related Skills and Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;1. Extensive knowledge of artificial intelligence, in particular the threats and complexities it poses to the major human rights challenges of our time is required.&lt;br&gt;2. Experience working on the impact of AI or other technology issues in Asia and fluency in an Asian language are desirable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;3. Strong commitment to understanding how technology can impact the rights of women, racial and ethnic minorities, children, older people, people with disabilities, people living in poverty and low-wage workers, and other populations whose rights may be disproportionately impacted by AI is desirable.&lt;br&gt;4. Proven track record of producing timely and high-quality written research and investigations, as well as editing experience is required.&lt;br&gt;5. Ability to present and defend complex technology-related issues and positions to officials in governments, companies, and other bodies and institutions is preferable.&lt;br&gt;6. Being comfortable with generating and executing research projects, and the curiosity and creativity to follow through and follow up is required.&lt;br&gt;7. Exceptionally strong research, analytical, writing, and editing skills are required.&lt;br&gt;8. Experience conducting challenging investigative research globally is required, as is the ability to dig deep and tenacity in finding hard-to-get information, sources and records.&lt;br&gt;9. Good oral and written communication skills in English, and strong public speaking skills, are required; proficiency in other languages, is highly desirable.&lt;br&gt;10. Experience with TV, radio, print, and social media is highly desirable.&lt;br&gt;11. Demonstrated ability to work independently as well as successfully with a team and across other teams is required.&lt;br&gt;12. Strong interpersonal skills to work collaboratively within HRW, as well as develop constructive relationships with NGO partners, and company and government officials are required.&lt;br&gt;13. Demonstrated awareness and sensitivity to the needs and concerns of individuals from diverse cultures, backgrounds, and orientations is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;: HRW offers competitive compensation and employer-paid benefits. HRW offers relocation assistance package and will assist employees in obtaining necessary work authorization in all listed locations except Nairobi, if required; citizens of all nationalities are encouraged to apply. If based in the United States, the salary range would be 88,000 – 104,000. Salary ranges outside of the United States vary based on location.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;: Please apply by December 13, 2026, by visiting our online job portal at careers.hrw.org and submitting a cover letter and CV or resume. No calls or email inquiries, please. Only complete applications will be reviewed and only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application submission, or if you require disability-related accommodation, please email ----- Rights Watch is strong because it is diverse&lt;/strong&gt;. We actively seek a diverse applicant pool and encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Human Rights Watch does not discriminate on the basis of disability, age, gender identity and expression, national origin, race and ethnicity, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, or criminal record. We welcome all kinds of diversity. Our employees include people who are parents and nonparents, the self-taught and university educated, and from a wide span of socio-economic backgrounds and perspectives on the world. Human Rights Watch is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Rights Watch &lt;/strong&gt;is an international human rights monitoring and advocacy organization known for its in-depth investigations, its incisive and timely reporting, its innovative and high-profile advocacy campaigns, and its success in changing the human rights-related policies and practices of influential governments and international institutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As the Forward Deployed Engineering Manager, you will lead the team that puts Auterion&#39;s robotic systems to work with customers in the field. We build complete systems: vehicles, sensors, onboard compute, radio links, autonomy software, and ground control. Your job is to understand how all of it fits together and to make it work in real missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead your team through the entire customer engagement, from discovery and integration to field trials and handover. You are not a hardware specialist. You are a systems engineer who can trace a problem across every layer of the system, lead people well, and earn the trust of demanding customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and grow a cross-functional team of Forward Deployed Engineers covering systems integration and software. Hire, coach, and develop your engineers. Build a culture of ownership and proactive problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the bar high for yourself and your team. Work directly with stakeholders across the company. You will have a close relationship with the CTO, CEO, VP of Engineering, and the engineering directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Own technical delivery of customer deployments in demanding, non-standard environments. This covers system configuration, connectivity, mission readiness, and operation under environmental constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the technical lead for high-stakes customer integrations. Ensure the full system works end to end: vehicle, payloads, onboard compute, communication links, autonomy software, and ground control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Troubleshooting:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose failures across hardware, firmware, software, and communications. Use logs, telemetry, and structured debugging to find root causes fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical contact for defense and enterprise customers. Translate operational requirements into deployment plans that account for system performance, link quality, power, and mission constraints. Run technical meetings, demos, and field days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feedback Loop &amp;amp; Release Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Product and R&amp;amp;D to feed field results and real-world edge cases back into the product. Coordinate with R&amp;amp;D on platform releases so customer deployments stay current and stable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years in technical roles in robotics, drones, autonomous vehicles, or comparable complex embedded systems. You understand the full system end to end and how a change in one subsystem affects the others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years managing a technical, customer-facing team (Field Engineers, Forward Deployed Engineers, Solutions Architects, or similar). You have dealt with underperformance and built team culture deliberately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working in Linux. You write Python, read C++, and use Git. You debug from logs and telemetry, not only at the bench.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand hardware at integration level: power, sensors, interfaces, and RF basics. You do not need to be a hardware designer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with field-deployed systems where &quot;turning it off and on again&quot; isn&#39;t always an option. Understanding of networking and radio communication is a major plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crisis Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to troubleshoot critical failures in the field under high pressure and with limited physical access to the hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Composure and credibility in front of demanding customers. You communicate clearly with engineers and decision-makers alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent English. German is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Authorization:&lt;/strong&gt; Must hold EU citizenship and be eligible to work in the European Union without restriction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, ArduPilot, or ROS2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in defense or government programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility for German security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;What Cognite is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Relentless&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;to Achieve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite operates at the forefront of industrial digitalization, building AI and data solutions that solve the world’s hardest, highest-impact problems. Our Moonshot is bold: unlock $100B in customer value by 2035, and redefine how global industry works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;How you’ll demonstrate &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Solutions Architect is responsible for the design of complex end to end solutions, merging our flagship products with the customer&#39;s portfolio, for both new and existing clients. You are a technical subject matter expert in all offerings across the professional and managed services catalog. From discovery through implementation, you will work closely with the sales team and the delivery teams, as well as our data scientists and customers to map out technical requirements and architect robust and familiar solutions. Through your work with our strategic customers, you will identify opportunities for new products and features, and work with our product managers and tech leads to continuously improve Cognite&#39;s SaaS offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a mix of consulting, architecture, and product development in a welcoming cross-functional team. Above all else, we strive to foster a supportive team environment where everyone is excited to share ideas, ask for help, and learn from each other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;The &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Impact&lt;/span&gt; you bring to Cognite&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As a Senior Solutions Architect, you will be an expert in how we implement our Cognite SaaS offerings and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your primary responsibility will be to work with project teams to map requirements for a quality implementation ensuring that:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right data visualization technology is used in the right way (E.g Power BI, Grafana, Plotly Dash)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right data transformation technology is used in the right way (E.g Databricks, Azure, GCP, AWS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The data is efficiently modeled and contextualized in Cognite Data Fusion (E.g graph and relational)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrations are well thought out and robustImportant quality criteria for the solution are met (E.g. CI/CD, logging, security)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational responsibility and support agreements for the delivered solution are clearly defined&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design overall technical solution and ensure technical fit within the customer ecosystem and target architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design integration and data model using Cognite data connectors, SQL, Python/Java and Rest APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible advisor to our customers and partners on Cognite Data Fusion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years experience as an application/data engineer/solution/enterprise architect or Machine learning engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in engineering, computer science, physics, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent demonstrated experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on in python as well as a good hands-on expertise with software development best practices.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a DevOps mindset, and experience with Git, CI/CD, deployment environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise integration, customer relationships or IT integration design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with operational data and customer business drivers in the heavy asset industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a public cloud, preferably AWS, GCP or Azure, including familiarity with network security concepts, identity providers and application hosting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with operations, including support and change control, as well as experience architecting centralized monitoring, logging and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have architectural skills dealing with data modeling and infrastructure solutions, such as classical data warehousing and big data architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience from the heavy asset industry (Oil &amp;amp; Gas, Energy, Manufacturing or Pharma) is preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consulting experience that allows you to confidently negotiate requirements with customers and colleague&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A snapshot of our many perks and benefits as a Cogniter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Join an organization of 60 different nationalities 🌐 with Diversity, Equality and Inclusion (DEI) in focus 🤝&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* A highly modern and fun working environment with sublime culture across the organization, follow us on Instagram @&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/cognitedata/&quot;&gt;cognitedata&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;📷 to know more&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Flat structure with direct access to decision-makers&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Opportunity to work with and learn from some of the best people on some of the most ambitious projects found anywhere, across industries, with cutting edge technology&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Join our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://hub.cognite.com/&quot;&gt;HUB&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;🗣️ to be part of the conversation directly with Cogniters and our partners.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Get access to private health services with Cognite Care.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Hungry? We’ve got your back. A subsidized lunch at the canteen is delivered by the chefs at Fornebuporten (Aker Tech House)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* Our own&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/ClGdwKGK7j7/&quot;&gt;Cognite exclusive coffee bar&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;☕ with the friendliest baristas is here to brew coffee for coffee lovers, tea for tea lovers, smoothie for smoothie lovers, and the baristas creative concoctions when the mood strikes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* We take your mental- and physical health seriously by having a broad health offering and a free membership to our fully-staffed gym on-site.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;* A pet lover? Get the chance to meet&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/p/ClljJ29gdk7/&quot;&gt;Spot&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;at the Robot Garden!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #666e99;&quot;&gt;Why Cognite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the forefront of Industrial AI, partnering with some of the world&#39;s leading industrial organisations to solve problems that actually matter at scale — not hypothetical ones. You&#39;ll join a collaborative, fast-moving environment where curiosity and ownership are the norm, not the exception. If you want delivery work you can point to and be proud of, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Cognite is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment at work and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive the same level of consideration for employment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

